  "final_message": "The account service and frontend are built, but I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't available here. I tested the API in-process with Flask's test client and ran the frontend build, which passes. I didn't open the frontend in a browser.\n\nWhat the API tests showed:\n- **Lockout:** after 5 failed sign-ins for a username, a sign-in with the right password gets 429 with `Retry-After: 900`.\n- **Admin:** `admin` can list the lock and unlock the username, and the user can then sign in.\n- **Access control:** a non-admin gets 403 on the admin routes, and a request with no token gets 401.\n- **Attempt limit:** after 20 sign-in attempts from one client in a minute, the next gets 429 with `Retry-After: 59`.\n\nBehaviours you might not expect:\n- **Client identity:** the attempt limit uses the client's IP address. Behind a reverse proxy, set `TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT` to the number of proxies, or every user will share one limit.\n- **Unknown usernames:** failed sign-ins for usernames that don't exist also count toward lockout, so they can't be told apart from real ones. Unlocking an unknown username still answers 200.\n- **Attempt-limit counting:** every sign-in attempt counts toward the 20-per-minute limit, whether it succeeds or fails.\n- **Admin password:** `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is read at startup. If it is unset or empty, admin sign-in is disabled.\n- **Additions beyond the spec:**\n  - `POST /api/auth/logout` backs the sign-out button.\n  - `GET /api/me` also returns `is_admin`.\n  - Tokens expire after 7 days.\n\nThe backend is in `backend/app.py`, with data in SQLite at `data/app.db`. The frontend is in `frontend/src`, styled with Tailwind v4. When sign-in is refused, the form shows whether it was the username lockout or the attempt limit, the time to try again and a live countdown.\n\nI also added a `.gitignore`. In `frontend/package.json` the build script is now `tsc && vite build`, so a type error fails the build.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
